    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d672">

                <pb facs="1367" n="1355" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-14T10:00:00+09:00">July 14, 1946—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 15—5:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1138. Uneasy truce continued, but indications were that constantly reported
                    isolated clashes could develop into open civil war. Mutual KMT-Communist
                    accusations of breaking cease-fire agreement of 7 June continued. Areas
                    principally affected are in Shansi, Shantung, and southern Honan.</p>
                <pb facs="1368" n="1356" xml:id="pg1356"/>
                <p>Reliable sources report constant Central Government air attacks against
                    Communists during period 30 June through 6 July. Chinese Air Force flew 81
                    missions using 153 aircraft. (Summary Military] Attaché’s] report for period 6
                    July through 12 July.) On 5 July, 4 aircraft, alleged Communist, strafed Yellow
                    River ferry crossing near Kaifeng.</p>
                <p>In late June, one B–24 aircraft of Chinese Air Force flew to Yenan and remained;
                    Communists claim crew deliberately joined their side. Government has ignored
                    Yenan claims, but specific Communist identification of unit (35th Squadron, 8th
                    Bombardment Group) and crew lends credence to Communist report. Communist
                    attacks in Tatung area of Shansi continued. In Tsinan area, Shantung,
                    Nationalist counterattacks east along railway had reached Choutsun on 9 July.
                    Concentration of 100,000 Communist troops north Kiangsu increased tension that
                    area.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
